# Line endings: every text file is stored with LF in the repository AND checked out with LF on every OS (eol=lf overrides
# core.autocrlf), so a tool or an editor that writes CRLF can never turn into a whole-file diff / merge conflict again
# (the spell-chess, horde-chess and crazyhouse branches did exactly that: ~20 existing files stored as CRLF).
# `text=auto` leaves real binaries alone; the explicit entries below make sure of the types this project ships.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Hooks run under sh: a CRLF checkout would break the shebang line.
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Binary: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.wasm binary
*.nnue binary
*.bin binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
